2026-10-28T09:08:21.1946736Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-28T09:08:21.1958987Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2036624Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2044596Z [0m
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2045188Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2045603Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2045785Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2046017Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2046474Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2046706Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2047087Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2047578Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2047738Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2048174Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2048559Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2048801Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2048994Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2049083Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2049207Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2049350Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2049490Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2049688Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2049762Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2049824Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2049910Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2050111Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2050387Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2055172Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2055268Z I will:
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2055364Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2055538Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2055892Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2056192Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2056410Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2056584Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2056744Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2057817Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2058114Z    /root
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2068052Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2068502Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2077691Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2078368Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2078704Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2079132Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2079790Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2101456Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2101936Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2110029Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2110506Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2110896Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2111013Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2111125Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2111245Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2111387Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2111623Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2111825Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2111919Z If you would like to
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2112085Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2112180Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2112311Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2112511Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2112610Z 
2026-10-28T09:08:21.2112700Z 
